\section{Problem Statement}
\label{sec:intro_problem}

Let $\vect{x} \in \R^n$ denote the state vector. The objective function is governed by:
\begin{equation}
    \label{eq:governing_state}
    J(\vect{x}) = \int_{0}^{T} \left( \vect{x}(t)^\top \mat{Q} \vect{x}(t) + \vect{u}(t)^\top \mat{R} \vect{u}(t) \right) \dd t.
\end{equation}
As formulated in \cref{eq:governing_state}, the minimization depends on weighting matrices $\mat{Q}$ and $\mat{R}$.

